The paper benchmarks vector search (HNSW in the browser vs. cloud vector databases). It mentions RAG only as context. It runs no experiments with a generator conditioning on retrieved text; it measures retrieval latency, memory, and recall only. Under E1, retrieval without a generator conditioning on it is not RAG. The abstract does not describe any generation component.

It could be argued as MAYBE because vector search is a RAG component, but the rules say to exclude retrieval without a generator.

{"decision": "EXCLUDE", "code": "E1", "reason": "Benchmarks vector search latency and recall only; no generator conditioning on retrieved text."}
